WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.739 --> 00:00:07.339
Have you ever watched the clock and calculated how much sleep you could still

2
00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:07.739
get?

3
00:00:07.739 --> 00:00:13.383
The harder you try to make sleep happen, the more frustrating being awake can

4
00:00:13.383 --> 00:00:13.786
feel.

5
00:00:14.151 --> 00:00:19.140
Sleep can vary from night to night. A difficult night deserves care, without

6
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.977
turning it into a judgment about how well you’re doing.

7
00:00:22.977 --> 00:00:28.060
You can make room for sleep through your schedule, environment, and habits.

8
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.024
But you can’t command an exact result.

9
00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:36.840
If watching the time adds pressure, consider moving the clock out of easy

10
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:37.259
view.

11
00:00:37.259 --> 00:00:42.763
If you’re lying awake and becoming frustrated, you could get up for a quiet

12
00:00:42.763 --> 00:00:48.267
activity in dim light and return when you feel sleepy, if it’s safe and

13
00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:48.660
practical.

14
00:00:49.025 --> 00:00:53.050
Persistent sleep problems deserve attention. They aren’t evidence that you

15
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.659
haven’t tried hard enough.

16
00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:58.683
A healthcare professional can consider possible causes and suitable treatment.

17
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:02.304
For adults with chronic insomnia, cognitive behavioral therapy for

18
00:01:02.304 --> 00:01:04.719
insomnia—called CBT-I—is an established treatment option.

19
00:01:05.084 --> 00:01:08.704
SteadierMind’s wind-down is a wellness activity, rather than CBT-I.

20
00:01:08.704 --> 00:01:12.727
Tonight, give yourself permission to support rest without grading your

21
00:01:12.727 --> 00:01:16.750
performance. And if difficulties continue, you can ask for help.
